+# http3
+
+`http3.Server` serves HTTP/3 through `logos/net/http.H3Server`. `Start` opens one UDP listener on the same port as the TCP listener. The router answers HTTP/3 requests with the same stages and replies as other versions.
+
+`H3Server` runs over the `github.com/quic-go/quic-go` transport. It clones the TLS configuration for UDP, requires TLS 1.3, and sets ALPN to `h3`.
+
+## Interface
+
+```lgo
+type Server struct {
+	Addr              string = ":8080"
+	Router            *web.Router
+	ReadHeaderTimeout time.Duration = 5 * time.Second
+	ShutdownGrace     time.Duration = 20 * time.Second
+	TLS               *tls.Config?
+	H2C               bool
+	H3                bool
+	// unexported fields
+}
+
+func (s *Server) AltSvc() web.Stage
+func (s *Server) Start(ctx context.Context) error
+func (s *Server) Serve(ctx context.Context, l net.Listener, conn net.PacketConn) error
+func (s *Server) Stop(ctx context.Context) error
+
+var ErrH3NeedsTLS = fault.New("http3.h3_needs_tls", fault.Internal, "HTTP/3 needs a TLS configuration.")
+var ErrListenUDP = fault.New("http3.listen_udp", fault.Internal, "The UDP listener failed to open.")
+var ErrH3Serve = fault.New("http3.h3_serve", fault.Internal, "The HTTP/3 server failed.")
+var ErrH3Shutdown = fault.New("http3.h3_shutdown", fault.Internal, "The HTTP/3 shutdown failed.")
+func Faults() []*fault.Error
+```
+
+The other fields keep the meaning that [web](web.md) gives them, except `ReadHeaderTimeout`, which bounds the TCP listener only. `H3` turns HTTP/3 on.
+
+## Requirements
+
+### Listener and discovery
+
+- `H3` MUST stay false unless the application wants HTTP/3.
+- When `H3` is true, `Start` MUST open one UDP listener on `Addr` before it returns.
+- The UDP listener MUST use the same port as the TCP listener.
+- When `Addr` holds port 0, `Start` MUST bind TCP first on port 0, then UDP on the bound TCP port.
+- On a UDP conflict `Start` MUST release both sockets and MUST try again a bounded number of times.
+- `Serve` MUST serve the caller sockets instead of binding `Addr`.
+- `Serve` MUST NOT close the caller sockets when it fails.
+- When `H3` is true and `TLS` is nil, `Start` MUST fail and MUST NOT listen.
+- The UDP listener MUST negotiate only ALPN `h3`.
+- The UDP listener MUST use TLS 1.3 with no older version.
+- `ReadHeaderTimeout` MUST bound the TCP listener header reads only.
+- `ReadHeaderTimeout` MUST NOT be presented as bounding HTTP/3 header reads.
+- The TCP listener MUST keep the ALPN list that [web](web.md) fixes.
+- Each HTTPS response MUST carry `Alt-Svc: h3=":<port>"; ma=2592000` while the UDP listener is open, with the actual UDP port.
+- A cleartext response MUST NOT carry that header.
+- A response when `H3` is false MUST NOT carry that header.
+- The router MUST run the same stages for an HTTP/3 request as for other versions.
+- The router MUST write the same replies for an HTTP/3 request as for other versions.
+- `AltSvc` MUST set `Alt-Svc` with the bound UDP port on an HTTPS request while the server runs.
+- The stage MUST skip a cleartext request, a stopped server and a server with `H3` false.
+- `Start` MUST NOT add the stage to the router itself.
+- When `H3` is false, `Start` MUST serve TCP only and open no UDP listener.
+
+### Limits and timeouts
+
+These limits and timeouts apply to the LoGOs backend that `http3.Server` uses.
+
+- The backend MUST use `http.DefaultMaxHeaderBytes` (1 MiB) because `http3.Server` sets no `MaxHeaderBytes`.
+- The backend MUST advertise this value in `SETTINGS_MAX_FIELD_SECTION_SIZE` (RFC 9114 section 7.2.4.1).
+- This value MUST limit the encoded request header block and the decoded field section separately. Each decoded field MUST count its name and value in bytes plus 32 bytes.
+- If either limit is exceeded, the backend MUST stop reading the stream with `H3_EXCESSIVE_LOAD` and MUST attempt status 431.
+- The backend MUST omit `SETTINGS_QPACK_MAX_TABLE_CAPACITY` and `SETTINGS_QPACK_BLOCKED_STREAMS`. Both MUST default to 0 (RFC 9204 section 5).
+- If a header block refers to the dynamic table, the backend MUST close the connection with `QPACK_DECOMPRESSION_FAILED`.
+- A client MUST keep at most 100 bidirectional streams and 100 unidirectional streams open per connection.
+- The backend MUST cap incoming streams at 100 bidirectional and 100 unidirectional per connection.
+- The initial QUIC receive window MUST be 1 MiB per stream and 1 MiB per connection (RFC 9000 section 4).
+- The QUIC send buffer MUST hold at most 1 MiB per stream. A write MUST wait for space if the buffer is full.
+- The backend MUST set the QUIC handshake timeout to 5 seconds.
+- After the QUIC handshake, the backend MUST wait up to 5 seconds for client SETTINGS. On timeout it MUST close the connection with `H3_MISSING_SETTINGS`.
+- The server MUST use a local idle timeout of 30 seconds. It MUST send no `max_idle_timeout` transport parameter or keep-alive packets.
+- If the client advertises a smaller nonzero idle timeout, the server MUST use that value. QUIC MUST set each handshake and idle timer to at least three times the probe timeout (RFC 9000 section 10.1).
+- The backend MUST set no separate request header deadline. A stream waiting for request headers MUST count against the bidirectional stream limit.
+- `Stop` MUST use a separate drain deadline. The QUIC idle timeout MUST remain in effect during the drain and MAY close an idle connection first.
+
+### Shutdown
+
+- `Stop` MUST close the UDP listener before it returns, after the drain or the timeout ends it.
+- `Stop` MUST send GOAWAY on HTTP/3 connections, then wait for open requests until `ShutdownGrace` ends (RFC 9114).
+- `Stop` MUST return at the caller deadline when that deadline is sooner.
+- `Stop` MUST close HTTP/3 connections when shutdown times out.
+- `Stop` of a server that is not started MUST return a nil error.
+- On each connection with an open HTTP/3 control stream, a graceful drain MUST send one GOAWAY frame.
+- The GOAWAY identifier MUST be the next client bidirectional stream ID after the highest admitted request stream. If the backend admitted no request stream, the identifier MUST be 0.
+- Once the drain starts, the backend MUST admit no new request streams. It MUST reject new request streams on open connections with `H3_REQUEST_REJECTED` so the client can retry the request.
+- The backend MUST reject request stream IDs at or above `2^62 - 4`.
+- The cap MUST leave room for the GOAWAY identifier in a variable-length integer.
+- The control stream MUST reject an attempt to send a GOAWAY identifier greater than the previous one.
+- The backend MUST wait for admitted requests to finish and for QUIC to acknowledge GOAWAY. If both complete and the connection remains open, it MUST close the connection with `H3_NO_ERROR`.
+- A client GOAWAY frame MUST NOT stop requests. If a client GOAWAY identifier exceeds the previous one, the backend MUST close the connection with `H3_ID_ERROR`.
+
+### Early data
+
+- The server MUST refuse 0-RTT early data, because early data replays and a replayed request could run twice.
+- When a client attempts TLS session resumption, the QUIC layer MUST clear the early data flag on the session. The server MUST accept no 0-RTT data and MUST keep no 0-RTT replay window.
+- The QUIC backend MUST issue no session tickets. The server MAY resume with a ticket from another issuer if the TLS configuration accepts it.
+- A restart MUST NOT drop the ability to resume a session established before the restart.
+- The TLS configuration MUST retain a valid ticket key for such a session, or recover its state with `UnwrapSession`.
+- `http3.Server` MUST NOT manage ticket key storage or rotation.
+- `SessionTicketsDisabled` on the effective TLS configuration MUST disable resumption.
+- Extended CONNECT over HTTP/3 MUST stay unbuilt in this server.
+- The server MUST answer an extended CONNECT request with 501 and MUST NOT pass it to the router.
+- `H3Server` MUST send `SETTINGS_ENABLE_CONNECT_PROTOCOL = 1`.
+- Peers MAY therefore attempt extended CONNECT.
+- The backend MUST answer extended CONNECT with 501 and MUST NOT call the request handler.
+
+### Faults
+
+- A nil `TLS` with `H3` MUST map to `http3.h3_needs_tls`.
+- A UDP listen failure MUST map to `http3.listen_udp` with the address in the cause.
+- An HTTP/3 serve failure MUST map to `http3.h3_serve` with the cause.
+- An HTTP/3 shutdown failure MUST map to `http3.h3_shutdown` with the cause.
+
+### Code table
+
+| Code | Kind | Message |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `http3.h3_needs_tls` | internal | "HTTP/3 needs a TLS configuration." |
+| `http3.listen_udp` | internal | "The UDP listener failed to open." |
+| `http3.h3_serve` | internal | "The HTTP/3 server failed." |
+| `http3.h3_shutdown` | internal | "The HTTP/3 shutdown failed." |
+
+## Errors
+
+- A nil `TLS` with `H3` MUST map to `http3.h3_needs_tls`.
+- A UDP listen failure MUST map to `http3.listen_udp` with the address in the cause.
+- An HTTP/3 serve failure MUST map to `http3.h3_serve` with the cause.
+- An HTTP/3 shutdown failure MUST map to `http3.h3_shutdown` with the cause. `Stop` then closes the HTTP/3 server and joins that error.
+- Public views MUST NOT carry addresses, ports or transport details.
+
